From 51c1611f91d61fb15e36abad640b15f73b1dfcfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:50:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): stop between setups by default (#1532)

A two-setup document posted as one program ran from Setup 1's last cut
straight into Setup 2's first, on a part still clamped for Setup 1. A new
document post option, Between setups, decides what posts at a setup
change: Pause (M0, the default), Optional stop (M1), Run straight on (the
old program), or One file per setup.

- The stop folds into the setup's last operation's after-action, with a
  PARAM SetupChange naming the next setup; independent of "Skip pauses
  and homes". A Go home at the change is refused by name.
- Fanuc lifts Z (G91 G28 Z0) and writes (SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>)
  before M0/M1; Tormach PathPilot now declares afterModes, lifts with
  G53 G0 and shows (MSG, SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>). A post without
  afterModes is refused at the change by name.
- One file per setup splits the mounts per setup; the one-file post
  refuses such a program by name.
- Project key post_options.between_setups (written only off default),
  setup-owned options compared for it, UI combo box, and the MCP post
  tool's between_setups argument through the undoable SetPostOptions.

Fixes #1532

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
